        "original_id": "50905001-11a2-59fb-8ebc-ab580bac2ee0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Kerrygold Irish Cream Liqueur\n- Organizations: Kerrygold, Ornua, Irish Dairy Board\n- Topics: trademark ownership, U.S. product introduction, company naming, agri-food co-operatives, dairy marketing\n\nFacts:\n- Kerrygold Irish Cream Liqueur was first introduced in the United States in 2014.\n- The trademark for Kerrygold Irish Cream Liqueur is owned by Kerrygold under Ornua.\n- Ornua was previously known as the Irish Dairy Board.\n- The name Ornua comes from the Irish phrase \"Ór Nua,\" meaning \"new gold.\"\n- Ornua is an Irish agri-food co-operative.\n- Ornua markets and sells dairy products on behalf of its members, which are Irish dairy processors and Irish dairy farmers.",
